Recommended Structure

Flexible Height Gallery
 ├── Title Label
 ├── Description Label (AutoHeight=true)
 ├── Status Label
 └── Date Label

Each lower control references the previous control’s height.


---

If You Already Use a Normal Vertical Gallery

You have 2 options:

Option 1 (Recommended)

Replace it with:

Flexible Height Gallery


Option 2

Manually calculate row height using formulas, but this is harder and less reliable.


---

Performance Tip

If descriptions are VERY long and many rows exist:

Avoid too many AutoHeight controls

Use pagination/filtering

Keep gallery optimized


Because flexible galleries can become slower with huge datasets.


---

Best Practice for SharePoint + Power Apps

For comments/descriptions:

Use:

Multiple lines of text in SharePoint

Flexible Height Gallery in Power Apps


This combination works best.

